# IYDT-GSRP four-phenomenology MultiPEM analyses

These decks combine seismic, acoustic, optical, and crater observations to
infer SUGAR log-yield and HOB. Rapid and complete assessments are provided with
fixed benchmark yields or errors-in-variables (EIV) yields for the applicable
phenomenologies.

| Directory | Yield treatment | Assessment |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `I-EIV-SUGAR-hob-0` | EIV | rapid calibration + event |
| `I-SUGAR-hob-0` | fixed | rapid calibration + event |
| `I-EIV-SUGAR-hob` | EIV | complete joint inference |
| `I-SUGAR-hob` | fixed | complete joint inference |

## Native prerequisites

```text
ln -s ../../../Applications/Code/IYDT-gsrp/Phenomenology Code
mkdir -p Opt
```

Run every matching single-phenomenology calibration before a four-phenomenology
deck. Stage rapid starting values as follows:

```text
cp ../Seismic/I-SUGAR-hob-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_1_0.RData
cp ../Acoustic/I-SUGAR-hob-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_2_0.RData
cp ../Optical/I-EIV-SUGAR-hob-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_3_eiv_0.RData
cp ../Optical/I-SUGAR-hob-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_3_0.RData
cp ../Crater/I-EIV-SUGAR-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_4_eiv_0.RData
cp ../Crater/I-SUGAR-0/opt.RData Opt/opt_4_0.RData
```

Stage complete-assessment starting values separately:

```text
cp ../Seismic/I-SUGAR-hob/opt.RData Opt/opt_1.RData
cp ../Acoustic/I-SUGAR-hob/opt.RData Opt/opt_2.RData
cp ../Optical/I-EIV-SUGAR-hob/opt.RData Opt/opt_3_eiv.RData
cp ../Optical/I-SUGAR-hob/opt.RData Opt/opt_3.RData
cp ../Crater/I-EIV-SUGAR/opt.RData Opt/opt_4_eiv.RData
cp ../Crater/I-SUGAR/opt.RData Opt/opt_4.RData
```

Each deck reads the subset matching its EIV/fixed and rapid/complete name.
Because `opt_files_in` is hard-coded, all referenced files must exist before the
deck reaches MLE optimization.

## Execution

For a rapid directory, run `runMPEM.r` and then `runMPEM_0.r` after successful
calibration. Before the event deck, always preserve the pristine calibration
`.RData` separately (for example, as `.RData-calibration`) for future event
analyses. Run native batch jobs in the background as described in `../README`.
For a complete directory, run only `runMPEM.r`; it estimates calibration and
new-event quantities jointly.

## Docker staging

Every source `opt.RData` remains in its producing job snapshot. Copy it from
`RESULTS/work/IYDT-gsrp/PHENOMENOLOGY/ANALYSIS/opt.RData` into the canonical
destinations above before creating the four-phenomenology Docker job. Job
creation then captures the populated `Opt` directory. Do not attempt to reuse
one results directory across different analysis paths.

The Docker analysis names begin `IYDT-gsrp/4-Phen/`; see
`../../../Runfiles-Docker/README` for job lifecycle, checkpoint, and resource
controls.
